    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1_1Type" kindref="compound">Type</ref> of vertex key for graphs that do not index their vertices.</para><para>This is the default vertex key type, <computeroutput>VKey</computeroutput> argument, for the <ref refid="classGraph" kindref="compound">Graph</ref> template. In order to index graph vertices you must provide at least the vertex key type which must have a copy constructor and a constructor that takes a vertex value argument. Depending on the index type obtained from <ref refid="structSawyer_1_1Container_1_1GraphIndexTraits" kindref="compound">GraphIndexTraits</ref>, this key type may need additional functionality such as a default constructor and a less-than operator or hashing function. </para>    </detaileddescription>
